  'articles-guide-a-an-the',
  'The Complete Guide to English Articles (a, an, the)',
  'Master the most confusing aspect of English grammar. Learn when to use a, an, the—or no article at all.',
  E'# The Complete Guide to English Articles (a, an, the)\n\nArticles are one of the hardest parts of English for non-native speakers. This guide will finally make them clear.\n\n## The Three Articles\n\n1. **a** - indefinite article (singular)\n2. **an** - indefinite article (singular, before vowel sounds)\n3. **the** - definite article\n\n## When to Use "A/An"\n\nUse indefinite articles when:\n\n### 1. Mentioning something for the first time\n\n✅ I saw **a** dog in the park.\n✅ She bought **an** umbrella.\n\n### 2. Talking about any member of a group\n\n✅ I need **a** pen. (any pen)\n✅ He is **a** teacher. (one of many teachers)\n\n### 3. With countable singular nouns\n\n✅ That is **a** good idea.\n❌ That is good idea.\n\n## "A" vs. "An"\n\nUse "an" before vowel **sounds** (not just vowel letters):\n\n✅ **an** apple\n✅ **an** honest man (silent "h")\n✅ **an** MBA\n✅ **an** hour\n\n✅ **a** university (starts with "yu" sound)\n✅ **a** European country\n✅ **a** one-way street\n\n## When to Use "The"\n\nUse the definite article when:\n\n### 1. Both speaker and listener know what you mean\n\n✅ I saw **the** dog again. (We talked about this dog before)\n✅ Close **the** door. (We both know which door)\n\n### 2. There is only one\n\n✅ **the** sun\n✅ **the** moon  \n✅ **the** President of the United States\n\n### 3. With superlatives\n\n✅ **the** best student\n✅ **the** most important factor\n\n### 4. With specific groups\n\n✅ **the** rich and **the** poor\n✅ **the** elderly\n\n## When to Use NO Article\n\n### 1. Plural nouns in general\n\n✅ **∅** Dogs are loyal. (dogs in general)\n✅ **∅** Students need support.\n\n### 2. Uncountable nouns in general\n\n✅ **∅** Water is essential.\n✅ **∅** Education is important.\n\n### 3. Countries, cities, streets (usually)\n\n✅ I live in **∅** France.\n✅ **∅** Paris is beautiful.\n✅ She lives on **∅** Main Street.\n\nExceptions:\n❌ **the** United States\n❌ **the** Philippines\n❌ **the** Netherlands\n\n### 4. Most possessive nouns\n\n✅ **∅** My book (not "the my book")\n✅ **∅** John''s car\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n### Mistake 1: Using articles with abstract nouns\n\n❌ The love is beautiful.\n✅ **∅** Love is beautiful.\n\n### Mistake 2: Forgetting articles with singular countable nouns\n\n❌ I am student.\n✅ I am **a** student.\n\n### Mistake 3: Using "the" for first mention\n\n❌ I bought **the** book yesterday.\n✅ I bought **a** book yesterday.\n\n## Practice Quiz\n\nFill in the blanks:\n\n1. I want to be ___ doctor.\n2. ___ moon is bright tonight.\n3. ___ dogs are friendly animals.\n4. She gave me ___ advice.\n5. That is ___ best movie I''ve seen.\n\n**Answers:** 1. a, 2. The, 3. ∅, 4. ∅, 5. the\n\n## Master Articles with Wrytt\n\nArticle errors are among the most common mistakes in student writing. Wrytt:\n\n- Detects every article error in your essay\n- Explains WHY it''s wrong\n- Creates quizzes to reinforce correct usage\n\n[Fix your article errors now →](/analyze)\n\n## Conclusion\n\nArticles seem simple but have complex rules. The key is:\n\n1. Know if the noun is countable/uncountable\n2. Know if it''s specific or general\n3. Practice with YOUR actual writing\n\n**Ready to master articles?** [Start with Wrytt →](/analyze)',
  'grammar',
  12,
  true
),
